- action(n1, "start process"): Hallucinates an undocumented step; the description states the process "begins with receiving applications".
- action(n7, "end process"): Hallucinates an undocumented step; the description states that after disposing, "the process comes to an end", indicating no terminal action node is required.
- actor(a_default, "Default", [...] ): Misidentifies the responsible participant as "Default"; the source explicitly assigns the process to "TS - Clerical Staff".
- precedence(i1, n1), precedence(n7, e1): Routes the control flow through undocumented nodes instead of directly linking the start to the first step ("receive applications") and the last step ("dispose applications") to the end, distorting the intended init-to-end progression.